### Step 7 tests - use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or copy into Postman).
### Change @base to your Render URL to repeat the tests on the hosted API.
@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Health -> 200
GET {{base}}/health

### 2. Read all -> 200 and an array
GET {{base}}/api/records

### 3. Create -> 201 (note the returned id)
POST {{base}}/api/records
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cracked window pane",
  "category": "Doors and Windows",
  "description": "The window in Room C2 has a crack across the glass.",
  "status": "Pending"
}

### 4. Read one -> 200 (change 10 to the id you got)
GET {{base}}/api/records/10

### 5. Update -> 200, same id
PUT {{base}}/api/records/10
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cracked window pane",
  "category": "Doors and Windows",
  "description": "The window in Room C2 has a crack across the glass.",
  "status": "In progress"
}

### 6. Delete -> 200 {"message":"Record deleted."}
DELETE {{base}}/api/records/10

### 7. Read the deleted id -> 404
GET {{base}}/api/records/10

### 8. Missing title -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/records
Content-Type: application/json

{ "category": "Electrical", "description": "No title was sent.", "status": "Pending" }

### 9. Invalid status -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/records
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Bad status", "category": "Electrical", "description": "Status is wrong.", "status": "Done" }

### 10. Malformed JSON -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/records
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "oops",

### 11. Invalid id -> 400
GET {{base}}/api/records/abc

### 12. Valid id that does not exist -> 404 (also try PUT and DELETE)
GET {{base}}/api/records/99999

### 13. Unknown route -> 404 JSON
GET {{base}}/nothing-here
